// v0_2_m4_errors.ynz — Intentional error triggers for ynz watch (v0.2-M4).
//
// These are NOT meant to compile cleanly. Each section demonstrates a watch
// infrastructure error path. Run with:
//   ynz watch --check examples/primantis-orders/v0_2_m4_errors.ynz
// and observe the diagnostic output.
//
// To simulate watch-specific infrastructure errors (file watcher init failure,
// no yinz.toml, RSS hard-stop), use the env vars documented below.
// --- Compile error: unknown identifier ---
// WHY: demonstrates that ynz watch renders compile errors identically to ynz build.
// Trigger: save this file with the line below uncommented.
// let x = unknownIdent
// --- Watch --check mode (build-only) ---
// WHY: with --check, ynz watch compiles but does NOT execute the program.
// Trigger: ynz watch --check examples/primantis-orders/v0_2_m4_errors.ynz
// Expected: "✓ Built in N ms" with no program output.
// --- RSS hard-stop (simulated) ---
// WHY: demonstrates the Layer 3 memory hard-stop message (WHAT/WHAT-INSTEAD/WHY format).
// Trigger: YNZ_WATCH_MAX_RSS_MB=1 ynz watch examples/primantis-orders/v0_2_m4_errors.ynz
// Expected: hard-stop message + exit code 2 within a few rebuilds.
// --- No yinz.toml in project mode ---
// WHY: demonstrates the WatchNoYinzToml error when watch is invoked on a directory
//      without a yinz.toml file.
// Trigger: ynz watch /tmp/  (or any directory without yinz.toml)
// Expected: error with WHAT/WHAT-INSTEAD/WHY + exit code 2.
// --- --json + --no-clear coexist (no error) ---
// WHY: verifies --json and --no-clear are not mutually exclusive.
// Trigger: ynz watch --json --no-clear examples/primantis-orders/v0_2_m4_errors.ynz
// Expected: NDJSON on stdout, no error about conflicting flags.

